    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup centered on speed and favorable matchups. Our highest efficiency play is **James Wood** (78.42), whose elite .420 xwOBA and aggressive base-running opportunity against the slow delivery of Chandler make him our cornerstone. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) follows closely, benefiting from a massive 14% boost via platoon advantage and an optimal #2 spot in the order, while **Brice Turang** (73.40) anchors our speed-focused strategy at the top of the lineup; his 19% boost from the SP skill match and high-leverage order position are critical given our emphasis on stolen bases. **Corbin Carroll** (73.03) also remains a set-and-forget start, with his elite speed profile holding firm despite a slight drag from the catcher's arm strength.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Cole Young** (49.98). While **Cole Young** benefits from a favorable SP matchup, his raw projection was edged out by the superior platoon and park factors bolstering **Kyle Karros** (57.47) and **Gabriel Moreno** (59.17). Similarly, **Austin Riley** (48.91) remained on the bench; despite his positive BvP history, the pitching skill of his opponent and a lower lineup slot suppressed his efficiency score below our active threshold. Owners should keep a close eye on **Alex Freeland**, whose 58.32 score is heavily reliant on a 19% SP skill boost and favorable wind; if weather conditions shift or the lineup order fluctuates, his value could pivot rapidly. We are essentially fading heavy, stationary bats today in favor of high-OBP, high-speed profiles like **James Wood** and **Brice Turang** to maximize our daily efficiency in this tight 5x5 race.",
